         <ab>
            
            
            <persName type="reg">
               <forename>John George</forename> <surname>Lidwell</surname>
            </persName>
            <persName type="full">John George Lidwell</persName>
            <date type="birth" when="1864"/>
            <date type="death" when="1919-07-23"/>
            <note type="gender">M</note>
         </ab>
         <div type="bio">
            <p>Dublin solicitor born in Fermanagh and a friend of <rs type="person" key="joyc49">JJ’s father</rs>. JJ sought his advice in the summer of 1912 after George Roberts of Maunsel &amp; Co. refused to issue <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Dubliners</name> without cuts. JJ’s letters to Lidwell do not survive. Lidwell had offices at 33 Upper Ormond Quay, a stone’s throw from the Ormond Hotel fictionalized in the ‘Sirens’ episode of <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Ulysses</name> and in which the solicitor features. JJ learned of his death in August 1919 from a <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Freeman’s Journal</name> clipping, which he enclosed to <rs type="person" key="weav76">Harriet Shaw Weaver</rs> as proof of the prophetic power of <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Ulysses</name>. A few weeks earlier, JJ had told her that ‘[a]s soon as I mention or include any person in it I hear of his or her death or departure or misfortune’. <hi rend="bold">Robert Spoo</hi> and <hi rend="bold">Ronan Crowley</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
      </body>
